  "original_html": "<h1 id=\"primary-heading\" class=\"sr-only\">Home</h1><div class=\"space-y-8\"><div class=\"space-y-6\"><div><form><div class=\"mb-5\"><div class=\"border-b border-slate-200\"><div class=\"sm:flex sm:items-baseline\"><h3 class=\"pb-4 text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-slate-900\">Test Form: </h3><div class=\"mt-4 sm:mt-0 sm:ml-10\"><nav class=\"-mb-px flex space-x-8\" aria-role=\"tabpanel\"></nav></div></div></div></div><div class=\"flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between\"><div class=\"w-full space-y-5 bg-white rounded-md shadow-md p-4\"><div><label for=\"paragraph[0]\" class=\"block text-sm font-medium text-slate-700\">\n  How might you introduce Say-Mean-Matter to your students? What about this framework do you think will be helpful for them? What might be challenging?\n  \n    <span class=\"text-red-600\">*</span></label><div class=\"mt-1\"><textarea class=\"shadow-sm focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-blue-500 block w-full sm:text-sm border-slate-300 rounded-md\" rows=\"4\" name=\"paragraph[0]\" id=\"paragraph[0]\" placeholder=\"\" aria-describedby=\"paragraph[0]-description\" required=\"required\" data-required=\"data-required\"></textarea></div></div><label for=\"85301ec5-d606-4c83-9794-2a66aded9652\" class=\"block text-sm font-medium text-slate-700\">\n  Upload an example you’ve created to try out They Say/I Say or Say-Mean-Matter with your students. This could be a handout or chart, a text plus directions for guiding students through the process, or a sample notebook/annotation page that models how the routine might look in practice.\n  \n    <span class=\"text-red-600\">*</span></label><div id=\"file-upload-85301ec5-d606-4c83-9794-2a66aded9652\" class=\"\"><div class=\"mt-1 border-dashed border-2 rounded-md bg-white h-44 p-4 flex justify-center items-center \"><div class=\"flex flex-col items-center\"><div class=\"flex justify-center items-center h-12\"><div class=\"space-y-1 text-center\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/sv